{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Not like the land of Egypt.</b> For it is a flat land, where a person can channel water to his fields from the rivers, as is done for a vegetable garden planted on the riverbank. But it [the Land of Israel] is a land of mountains and valleys, and a person cannot irrigate it except with the rain of heaven — <b>it drinks water from the rain</b> — and you always need the Holy One, blessed be He. Therefore He warned you about His commandments, so that He may bring you rain in its season."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:47.653275290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}